+
+## `recover-errors` tests
+
+`//@ recover-errors` tests check the error recovery of diagnostic runs: `aeneas` is called
+without `-abort-on-error`, must report every error, drop the declarations (or bodies) it cannot
+translate, translate the others and exit with status 1 (an uncaught exception exits with status 2
+and fails the test). The output of the `aeneas` call is recorded like for `known-failure` tests,
+and the generated files can be checked by the backend like the files of any other test.
+
+## Separate compilation tests
+
+The separate compilation options (`-canonical-names`, `-emit-manifest`, `-external`,
+`-diagnostic-manifest`) need several `charon`/`aeneas` calls per test. Their tests are the scripts
+of `tests/separate-compilation/`, run by `make separate-compilation-tests` (part of `make test`).
